summary:
  The podcast engine's exec handler goes back to taking two arguments, so
  the failure branch reads a name nothing declared and every failed
  download throws before the slot is freed.

history:
  Found 2026-09-05 reading PodcastEngine.qml. handleExec(cmd, stdout) had
  two parameters and its download-failure branch logged
  (stderr || "").trim() — stderr was declared nowhere, not in the engine
  and not on main.qml's root. In QML a bare undeclared name is a
  ReferenceError, so a curl that came back without __POD_OK__ (a 404, a
  dropped connection, a full disk) threw on the console.warn line and
  never reached the lines that clear _podDownloadKey, _podDownloadTitle
  and _podDownloadMeta. One failed transfer and no episode downloaded
  again until the widget was restarted, with nothing on screen to say
  why. The success path never touched stderr, which is how the tests
  stayed green. This mutant puts the two-argument signature back.

target:
  package/contents/ui/PodcastEngine.qml

find:
      function handleExec(cmd, stdout, stderr) {

replace:
      function handleExec(cmd, stdout) {

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_podcastengine.qml
  test_a_failed_download_frees_the_slot_and_names_the_reason: the
  handler must return true on a failed POD_DL and leave the slot empty.
  Line-neutral.
